# Behaviour of the watch application. The drivers it links are chosen in
# firmware/lib/Kconfig.

config CB91AI_WATCH_DISPLAY_SECONDS
	int "How long the display stays lit after a wake-up, in seconds"
	default 10
	range 1 15
	help
	  EF-44: the display is the first item of the energy budget, so it is
	  lit on demand and goes back to standby by itself.

config CB91AI_WATCH_ADV_ALWAYS
	bool "Advertise all the time, slowly (development)"
	help
	  In Cobalt Link, the product keeps its radio
	  silent and advertises for a reason only (a note, a sync by hand).
	  The development build advertises for good, fast for 30 s after
	  boot, a disconnection or a call, slow (1 s) otherwise, as the
	  self-test does: the PC then always finds a sealed watch.

config CB91AI_WATCH_LINK_OPEN
	bool "Cobalt Link without pairing (development)"
	help
	  The service is meant for an encrypted, authenticated link only
	  (the Cobalt Link specification). Until the pairing of phase
	  S exists, the development build opens it, as SMP is open.

config CB91AI_WATCH_DEBUG_SERVICE
	bool "Debug service: status line and time (development)"
	help
	  The status line and the time characteristic of the self-test, with
	  its UUIDs, so that ble_update.py and cobalt_time.py work on the
	  watch as they are (src/debug.c).

config CB91AI_WATCH_DEBUG_TAKE
	bool "Takes started by the PC harness (development)"
	help
	  Cobalt Link key 0x7F: a take of a set length, without the voice
	  detector, as if ALARM had been held, so that the harness checks the
	  whole chain on a sealed watch, a hundred notes in a row
	  (tools/cobalt_link.py hundred). Never in the product.

config CB91AI_WATCH_DEBUG_JOURNAL
	bool "The journal's period set by the PC harness (development)"
	help
	  Cobalt Link key 0x7D: the period of the journal of the temperature
	  and the cell (lot T1), 1 to 600 s until the next boot, so that the
	  harness fills pages and sectors in minutes
	  (tools/cobalt_link.py --period 5 journal). Never in the product.

config CB91AI_WATCH_DEBUG_DAILY
	bool "The daily call's period set by the PC harness (development)"
	help
	  Cobalt Link key 0x7E: the period of the daily call (the watch calls
	  the phone after a day without any contact), 60 to 86400 s until the
	  next boot, so that the harness sees it come in minutes
	  (tools/cobalt_link.py --daily 60 daily). Never in the product.

config CB91AI_WATCH_DEBUG_TRIAL
	bool "The trial of the calls (development, lot N1a)"
	depends on CB91AI_WATCH_ADV_ALWAYS
	help
	  Cobalt Link key 0x7A: for a time the phone or the harness sets, the
	  radio behaves as the product's, silent between its calls, and the
	  watch times each call from its first advertisement to the connection
	  of the phone, which reads it back: how fast a phone comes back in the
	  background (risk R11, app/android probe, tools/cobalt_link.py trial).
	  Never in the product.

config CB91AI_WATCH_DEBUG_WRIST
	bool "The wrist's tuning set by the PC harness (development)"
	help
	  Cobalt Link key 0x7C: the thresholds of the accelerometer for the
	  raise of the wrist and the double tap (lot D4), read and set again
	  at once, so that they are tuned at the wrist without a new image
	  (tools/cobalt_link.py wrist). Never in the product.

config CB91AI_WATCH_DEBUG_PASSKEY
	int "A fixed pairing code for the bench (development), 0: drawn at random"
	default 0
	range 0 99999
	help
	  The code of a pairing, shown on the glass as always, fixed instead
	  of drawn from the hardware generator: the PC of the bench pairs with
	  no one to read the glass (tools/ble_pair.py, lot S2), then installs
	  and tries a product image, whose SMP and Cobalt Link ask for the
	  authenticated link. Never in the product: its code is drawn at
	  random at every pairing, and read on the glass.

config CB91AI_WATCH_NOTE_MAX_S
	int "The longest take, in seconds"
	default 120
	range 10 300
	help
	  A take held past half a second shows "rEC" and runs on by itself
	  until a press of ALARM (2026-09-24), 3 s after the last
	  word, or this long. The voice goes straight to the 1 MB storage
	  flash, about 8 min of LC3 at 16 kbit/s in all: the 15 s of EF-23
	  came from the RAM of the V1. The watch keeps this much erased ahead
	  of the notes (59 sectors of 4 KB for 120 s), hence the bound.

config CB91AI_WATCH_CONFIRM_WAIT_S
	int "How long an image in test waits for its confirmation, in seconds"
	default 600
	range 120 3600
	help
	  The watch never confirms itself: the host confirms a new image over
	  SMP once it finds it running, which proves the way back works. An
	  image still in test after this long reboots, and MCUboot starts the
	  previous one again (src/update.c).

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
